\DOC ENSURES_WHILE_UP_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_WHILE_UP_TAC : term -> term -> term -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Reduces an {ensures} goal about a counted-up loop to a single conjunctive goal
containing a nonzero-trip-count side condition together with {ensures} subgoals
for loop entry, body, backedge and exit.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes four {term} arguments: a bound {t}, the number of loop
iterations; two program-counter terms {pc1} and {pc2} marking the loop's
body-start and backedge/body-end labels; and a loop invariant of the form
{\i s. ...}, parameterised by the iteration counter {i} and the machine state.
Applied to an {ensures} goal with precondition {pre}, postcondition {post} and
frame {frame}, it yields one subgoal whose conclusion conjoins: {~(t = 0)}; an
{ensures} from {pre} to the invariant at {0} at {pc1}; a quantified body step
from the invariant at {i} at {pc1} to the invariant at {i + 1} at {pc2}; a
quantified backedge step carrying the invariant at {i} from {pc2} back to
{pc1}; and an {ensures} from the invariant at {t} at {pc2} to {post}. Every
component retains the original frame ({MAYCHANGE}) component.
{
   A ?- ensures ... pre post frame
   ================================================  ENSURES_WHILE_UP_TAC `t` `pc1` `pc2` `\i s. ...`
   A ?- ~(t = 0) /\
        ensures ... /\
        (forall i. i < t /\ ~(i = t) /\ ~(t = 0) /\ 0 < t ==> ensures ...) /\
        (forall i. 0 < i /\ i < t /\ ~(i = t) /\ ~(i = 0) /\ ~(t = 0) /\ 0 < t
                   ==> ensures ...) /\
        ensures ...
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single-subgoal transformation, on {ensures}
goals for x86 machine-code loops.

\ENDDOC
